  "result": "The O3 lesson is written, along with a five-item quiz and its key.\n\n- **Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory.html`, set to 10 minutes. It covers four things:\n  - the context window and why every step re-sends the whole history;\n  - what is kept between steps versus between sessions;\n  - retrieval versus notes, with a short Python example;\n  - a worked token-cost calculation, with practice checks and a warm-up on the agent loop.\n- **Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key in `keys/0002.json`. It is ready whenever you want to take it.\n- **Notes and sources:** I added `RESOURCES.md` with the three sources I cited, and updated `NOTES.md`.\n\n- **Source checking:** I read the web results from search only. I did not open the Anthropic and Weng pages in full, so the lesson's claims rest on those search excerpts.\n- **Reading time:** I didn't count the words, so I can't confirm the lesson lands inside the 10-minute estimate.\n- **Not covered:** the lesson doesn't mention prompt caching, which lowers the price of re-sent tokens but not how much of the window they fill.\n- **Misconception ids:** I didn't map the quiz distractors to existing misconception ids, because I couldn't confirm what those ids mean.\n\nAsk me about anything in the lesson that is unclear.\n\nWhich community should I list for testing agent-design skills, since `RESOURCES.md` has none yet?",
